Let $X$ be a smooth projective complex threefold, $H$ an ample integral divisor, and $B_0\in N^1(X)_{\mathbb Q}$. There are constants $k\in\mathbb Q_{\geq0}$ and $R_*>0$, depending only on $(X,H,B_0)$, such that every finite-slope $\nu_{a,b}$-semistable $E\in\mathcal B_{H,B_0+bH}$ with $\nu_{a,b}(E)=0$ satisfies $$\label{eq:intro-corrected}
 \mathop{\mathrm{ch}}_3^{B_0+bH}(E)
 \leq \left(\frac{a^2}{6}+k\right)H^2\mathop{\mathrm{ch}}_1^{B_0+bH}(E)
 \qquad(a>0,\ b\in\mathbb R).$$ For the same fixed data, the stronger bound $$\label{eq:intro-tail}
 \mathop{\mathrm{ch}}_3^{B_0+bH}(E)
 \leq \frac{a^2}{6}H^2\mathop{\mathrm{ch}}_1^{B_0+bH}(E)$$ holds whenever $a>R_*$, for every $b\in\mathbb R$.

Let $X$ be a smooth projective threefold. Rational Chern characters identify its numerical Grothendieck group with $$\label{eq:full-numerical-lattice}
 K_{\mathrm{num}}(X)_\mathbb Q\simeq
 \mathbb Q\oplus N^1(X)_\mathbb Q\oplus N_1(X)_\mathbb Q\oplus\mathbb Q.$$ Products of numerical divisor classes span this space. Given a real ample class $H_*$, there are very ample line bundles $L_1,\ldots,L_q$ whose classes form a basis of $N^1(X)_\mathbb R$ and positive numbers $s_1,\ldots,s_q$ with $H_*=\sum_hs_hL_h$. For the product embedding $$\label{eq:product-embedding}
 i:X\hookrightarrow Y=\prod_{h=1}^q\mathbb P^{d_h},
 \qquad d_h=h^0(X,L_h)-1,$$ the pushforward $i_*:K_{\mathrm{num}}(X)_\mathbb R\to K_{\mathrm{num}}(Y)_\mathbb R$ is injective.

Let $Y=\prod_{h=1}^q\mathbb P^{d_h}$, put $\xi_h=c_1(\mathcal O_h(1))$, and fix $s_h>0$. There is a continuous family of numerical stability conditions $(U_R,\mathcal R_R)$ for $R\ge1$ with $$U_R(u)=-\int_Ye^{-iR\sum_hs_h\xi_h}\mathop{\mathrm{ch}}(u).$$ All point sheaves are stable of phase $1$. Write $\mathop{\mathrm{ch}}(u)=\sum_{\mathbf j}u_{\mathbf j}\xi^{\mathbf j}$, where $0\le j_h\le d_h$, and set $$\label{eq:ambient-scaled-coordinates}
 (M_Ru)_{\mathbf j}=
 u_{\mathbf j}\prod_h(Rs_h)^{d_h-j_h}.$$ For a fixed Euclidean norm there is $D>0$, independent of $R$, such that $$\label{eq:ambient-support}
 \|M_Ru\|\le D|U_R(u)|\qquad
 (u\text{ the class of an }\mathcal R_R\text{-semistable object}).$$ For every $\mathbf e\in\mathbb Z^q$, $$\label{eq:ambient-twist-distance}
 d(\mathcal R_R,\mathcal R_R\otimes\mathcal O_Y(\mathbf e))
 \le\sum_h\frac{d_h|e_h|}{\pi Rs_h}.$$

Let $V$ be a smooth projective variety of dimension $n\ge2$, and let $\mathcal R$ be a locally finite slicing in which every point sheaf is stable of phase $1$. Then $$\begin{aligned}
 \mathcal R(0,1]&\subset D^{[-n+1,0]}(V),
 &\mathop{\mathrm{Coh}}(V)&\subset\mathcal R(1-n,1],\label{eq:geometric-range}\\
 D^{\le-n}(V)&\subset\mathcal R(>0),
 &\mathcal R(>0)&\subset D^{\le0}(V).\label{eq:geometric-aisles}
\end{aligned}$$ The sheaf $\mathcal H^{-n+1}(E)$ is torsion-free for $E\in\mathcal R(0,1]$. Moreover, $\mathcal H^0(E)$ is zero-dimensional for $E\in\mathcal R(1)$.

Every $E\in\mathcal C$ has cohomology in degrees $[-2,0]$, its sheaf $\mathcal H^{-2}(E)$ is torsion-free, and $$\label{eq:heart-sign-bounds}
 m^+_{H,B}(\mathcal H^{-2}(E))\le-c,
 \qquad m^-_{H,B}(\mathcal H^0(E))>c.$$ A bound for a zero sheaf is vacuous.

We have $$\label{eq:first-tilt-phase-range}
 \mathcal B\subset\mathcal P(-1,1].$$ Consequently $$\mathcal T_0=\mathcal B\cap\mathcal P(0,1],\qquad
 \mathcal F_0=\mathcal B\cap\mathcal P(-1,0]$$ is a torsion pair in $\mathcal B$, and $\mathcal C=\langle\mathcal F_0[1],\mathcal T_0\rangle$.

Let $a>0$, let $B$ be real, and let $E\in\mathcal B_{H,B}$ be tilt-semistable of finite slope $u$. There are a zero-dimensional sheaf $T_0$ and a distinguished triangle $$\label{eq:tilt-dual-triangle}
 \widetilde E\longrightarrow\mathbb D(E)\longrightarrow T_0[-1]
 \longrightarrow\widetilde E[1],$$ where $\widetilde E\in\mathcal B_{H,-B}$ is tilt-semistable of slope $-u$. At twists $B$ and $-B$ respectively their coordinates are related by $$\label{eq:tilt-dual-characters}
 (r,d,w,z)(\widetilde E)
   =\bigl(-r(E),d_B(E),-w_B(E),z_B(E)+\operatorname{length}(T_0)/h\bigr).$$ Moreover $\widetilde E=\tau^{\le0}\mathbb D(E)$ for the ordinary cohomological truncation.

Let $G$ be a slope-semistable torsion-free sheaf of rank $r>0$ on $X$. For a very general smooth $S\in|H|$, restrict $G$ and refine its slope Harder–Narasimhan filtration into slope-stable torsion-free factors $G_i$, with ranks $r_i$ and normalized slopes $\mu_i$. Then $$\label{eq:restriction-variance}
 \sum_i r_i\bigl(\mu_i-\mu(G)\bigr)^2\le r\xi_G.$$ The same assertion holds for a slope-semistable torsion-free sheaf on $S$, restricted to a very general smooth $C_m\in|mH|_S$, for every positive integer $m$.*

*More generally, restrict a finite filtration with semistable torsion-free factors and refine each restricted factor separately. From $X$ to $S$, for any fixed divisor twist $T$ on $X$, restricted to $S$, the increases in $\sum_i r_i\mu_T(G_i)^2$ and in $\sum_i r_i\delta_{G_i}^T$ are equal and lie between zero and the original sum $\sum_G r(G)\xi_G$. From $S$ to $C_m$, the same upper bound holds for the increase of the second slope moment, using any fixed divisor twist on $S$ and its restriction to $C_m$. The concatenated filtration need not be the Harder–Narasimhan filtration of the whole restriction.

Let $Y$ range over the compact families of curves or surfaces in Lemma <a href="#lem:uniform-sections" data-reference-type="ref" data-reference="lem:uniform-sections">23</a>, with real dimension $n$. Write $\Delta_{\mathrm{sc}}$ for the nonnegative scalar Laplacian. Its heat kernel satisfies $$0\le k_s(x,y)\le C s^{-n/2}\qquad(0<s\le1).$$ For any Hermitian vector bundle with metric connection $
abla$, put $L=
abla^*
abla+1$. The kernel $K_s(x,y)$ of $e^{-sL}$ satisfies $$\label{eq:connection-heat}
 \|K_s(x,y)\|_{\mathrm{op}}\le C s^{-n/2}
 \qquad(s>0),$$ with a constant independent of the bundle, its rank, and its connection.

Let $Y$ be one of the curves or surfaces in Lemma <a href="#lem:uniform-sections" data-reference-type="ref" data-reference="lem:uniform-sections">23</a>, let $G$ be a slope-stable torsion-free sheaf on $Y$, and let $J\subset G$ have rank $q$. Then $$\label{eq:subsheaf-sections}
 h^0(Y,J)\le Cq\bigl(1+\mu(G)_+\bigr)^{\dim Y},
 \qquad x_+=\max\{x,0\},$$ where $C$ depends only on the chosen geometric families. The same bound applies to subsheaves of a stable dual bundle tensored with a line bundle, using the slope of that twisted bundle.

Let $S$ be one of the surfaces in Lemma <a href="#lem:uniform-sections" data-reference-type="ref" data-reference="lem:uniform-sections">23</a>. Let $\mathcal V$ be a Hermitian vector bundle with metric connection, $L=
abla^*
abla+1$, and let $P$ be a bounded measurable nonnegative selfadjoint endomorphism of $\mathcal V$. If a finite-dimensional subspace $U$ of the form domain of $L$ satisfies $$\label{eq:spectral-form-hypothesis}
 \langle Lu,uangle\le\langle Pu,uangle\qquad(u\in U),$$ then $$\label{eq:matrix-spectral-bound}
 \dim U\le C\int_S\operatorname{tr}(P^2).$$ The constant is independent of $\mathcal V$, its rank, $
abla$, and $P$.

Let $X$ be a smooth projective complex threefold, let $H$ be very ample, and let $B_0$ be a rational divisor class with $H^2B_0=0$. There are constants $A>0$ and $C\geq0$, depending only on $X,H,B_0$, such that, for every $b\in\mathbb R$ and every finite-slope $\nu_{A,b}$-semistable object $E\in\mathcal B_{H,B_0+bH}$ with $\nu_{A,b}(E)=0$, $$\label{eq:apex-estimate}
 z_B(E)-\frac{A^2}{6}d_B(E)
 \leq C\bigl(d_B(E)-A|r(E)|\bigr),\qquad B=B_0+bH.$$ The same constants can be chosen for $B_0$ and $-B_0$.

There are positive integers $j,j_2$ and a constant $C_0$, determined by $X,H,D$, with the following property. After choosing and shrinking a model of this fixed geometry over a finitely generated integral subring of $\mathbb C$, every smooth geometric fiber in characteristic $p$ and every $|b|\leq1$ satisfy the following assertion, for either $L=L_p$ or $L=L'_p$: $$G_{p,L}=F_*(K_X^{1-p}\otimes L^{-1})$$ has a presentation $$\label{eq:frobenius-presentation}
 0\longrightarrow K_{p,L}\longrightarrow\mathcal O_X(-j)^{N_{p,L}}
 \longrightarrow G_{p,L}\longrightarrow0,
 \qquad N_{p,L}\leq C_0p^3,$$ where $K_{p,L}(j_2)$ is generated by its global sections.

On a smooth geometric fiber in the preceding lemma, let $P_1$ be a perfect complex with ordinary cohomology in degrees $[-1,0]$. If $$H^0\bigl(\mathcal H^{-1}(P_1)(j_2)\bigr)=0,$$ then, for either $L=L_p$ or $L=L'_p$, $$\label{eq:frobenius-section-transfer}
 h^0(F^*P_1\otimes L)
 \leq C_0p^3h^0(P_1(j)).$$ The twists $j,j_2$ and the constant $C_0$ are those chosen from the fixed geometry in Lemma <a href="#lem:frobenius-presentation" data-reference-type="ref" data-reference="lem:frobenius-presentation">29</a>.

Let $E\in\mathcal B_{H,B_0+bH}$ be finite-slope $\nu_{A,b}$-semistable with $\nu_{A,b}(E)=0$ and $|b|\leq1$. Put $B=B_0+bH$ and $e=d_B(E)-A|r(E)|$. For $r(E)\geq0$, take $P$ from <a href="#eq:positive-residual-triangle" data-reference-type="eqref" data-reference="eq:positive-residual-triangle">[eq:positive-residual-triangle]</a> and put $V_P=\mathcal H^{-1}(P)$. For $r(E)\leq0$, use the decomposition <a href="#eq:negative-residual-triangle" data-reference-type="eqref" data-reference="eq:negative-residual-triangle">[eq:negative-residual-triangle]</a> and put $V=\mathcal H^{-1}(E)$. There is a constant $C_3$, independent of $E,b$, such that $$\label{eq:residual-sections}
 \begin{aligned}
 h^0(P(j))&\leq C_3e &&\text{for the positive decomposition},\\
 h^0(E(j))&\leq C_3e &&\text{for the negative decomposition}.
 \end{aligned}$$ Moreover $$\label{eq:negative-cohomology-vanishing}
 \begin{aligned}
 H^0(V_P(j_2))&=0&&\text{in the positive decomposition},\\
 H^0(V(j_2))&=0&&\text{in the negative decomposition}.
 \end{aligned}$$

Fix a smooth projective complex threefold $X$, an integral ample class $H$, and $B_0\in N^1(X)_{\mathbb Q}$. Suppose that there are $A>0$ and $C\ge0$ such that every finite-slope tilt-semistable object of slope zero at $(A,b)$, for every $b\in\mathbb R$, satisfies $$\label{eq:wall-apex-input}
 D_A(E)\le C S_A(E).$$ Then, with $$\label{eq:wall-constants}
 R_0=A+\frac{3C}{A},\qquad
 k_0=\max\left\{C+\frac{A^2}{6},\frac{CR_0}{A}\right\},$$ every finite-slope tilt-semistable object of slope zero at $(a,b)$ satisfies $D_a(E)\le k_0d_b(E)$ for all $a>0,b\in\mathbb R$, and $D_a(E)\le0$ whenever $a>R_0$.
